## Conversation
User asked to enable the three newly-enabled Copilot models (OpenAI
GPT-5.6 Luna, Sol, Terra) in the litellm config, and mid-task asked to
also remove gpt-5-5. Then asked to commit with the conventional-commits
skill.

## Actions
- Discovered exact upstream IDs (gpt-5.6-luna/sol/terra) by calling
  https://api.githubcopilot.com/models from inside the litellm
  container using the token in
  /root/.config/litellm/github_copilot/api-key.json
- Added the three models to configs/litellm/config.yaml; removed
  gpt-5-5; restarted the proxy after each config change
- Verified all three models plus claude-fable-5 return "ok" via both
  /v1/chat/completions and /v1/messages

## Errors & Mistakes
- First attempt (plain registration copying the gpt-5-5 entry) failed:
  Copilot returned "missing Editor-Version header for IDE auth" for ALL
  GPT models including the old gpt-5-5, on both routes. Claude models
  were unaffected
- Second attempt used a YAML merge key (<<: *copilot_headers) for the
  header block; go-yq parses "<<" literally (YAML 1.2) even though
