## Hints for Future Agents
- Copilot GPT-5.6 models are Responses-API-only. LiteLLM's gate
  github_copilot_supports_responses_api() (responses/transformation.py)
  routes unknown models to chat; per-deployment "model_info: mode:
  responses" in config.yaml flips it. New Copilot models will not be in
  the image's model_cost registry, so expect to set this for future
  additions
- The chat transformation adds Copilot default headers inside a
  try/except that silently passes on GetAPIKeyError; GPT entries carry
  an explicit Editor-Version extra_header to be safe. Claude entries
  work without it
- To list current upstream Copilot model IDs: exec python in the
  litellm container, read api-key.json token, GET
  https://api.githubcopilot.com/models with Editor-Version and
  Copilot-Integration-Id headers

## Codebase Discoveries
- Both github_copilot chat and responses transformations auto-detect
  vision content and set the vision header themselves; the configured
  Copilot-Vision-Request: "true" extra_header forces it on every
  request (pre-existing behavior, kept for consistency)
- gpt-5-5 was already broken on the current image (same missing-header
  error); the litellm-proxy.sh test commands only ever exercised
  claude-sonnet-4-6 and GLM, so this went unnoticed

